⌈ Runtime data of a Part.⌉
⌈ Parts are either leaves (a user-supplied handler) or containers (a handler that routes mevents to children).⌉
⌈ `handler` is called as handler (eh, mev).⌉
⌈ `instance_data` is private to the leaf; the handler finds it again each time it is invoked.⌉
⌈ `visit_queue` (containers only) holds the children that have been sent a mevent, once for each mevent.⌉
⌈ `tick` is a function (eh) that continues the processing of an active part. make_container sets it to container_tick; the programmer supplies it to make_leaf.⌉
⌈ `reset` is a function (eh) that puts the part back into a known state. make_container sets it to container_reset; the programmer supplies it to make_leaf.⌉
⌈ Eh_States :: enum { idle, active }⌉
defobj Eh {
        • name ⇐ “”
        • inq ⇐ #freshQueue ()
        • outq ⇐ #freshQueue ()
        • owner ⇐ ϕ
        • children ⇐ []
        • visit_queue ⇐ #freshQueue ()
        • connections ⇐ []
        • handler ⇐ ϕ
        • tick ⇐ ϕ
        • reset ⇐ ϕ
        • instance_data ⇐ ϕ
        • arg ⇐ “”
        • state ⇐ “idle”
        • vip ⇐ ⊥
}
